item.p:
in surface waters and in a 3m-wide strip alongside surface waters, whereby the strip alongside watercourses for which a space for waters has been specified in accordance with Article 41a WPO
SR 814.201 or for which a space for waters has been expressly dispensed with under 41a paragraph 5 WPO is measured from the shore line, and in the case of other watercourses and standing waters from the top edge of the bank in accordance with the buffer strip information sheet «Measuring and managing buffers strips correctly», KIP/PIOCH 2009
The information sheet may be obtained (not in English) from Agridea, 8315 Lindau. ;

the safety data sheet or the safety data sheets under Article 20 the Chemicals Ordinance of 5 June 2015

  SR 813.11
	;

Toxic equivalency as recommended by the World Health Organisation (WHO) following a consultation of experts in 2005. Reference: Martin van den Berg et al. (2006) The 2005 World Health Organization Re-evaluation of Human and Mammalian Toxic Equivalency Factors for Dioxins and Dioxin-Like Compounds. Toxicological science 93(2):223–241; 
							https://doi.org/10.1093/toxsci/kfl055
						.

Toxic equivalency as recommended by the World Health Organisation (WHO) following a consultation of experts in 2005. Reference: Martin van den Berg et al. (2006) The 2005 World Health Organization Re-evaluation of Human and Mammalian Toxic Equivalency Factors for Dioxins and Dioxin-Like Compounds. Toxicological science93(2):223–241; 
							https://doi.org/10.1093/toxsci/kfl055
						.

Toxic equivalency as recommended by the World Health Organisation (WHO) following a consultation of experts in 2005. Referenz: Martin van den Berg et al. (2006) The 2005 World Health Organization Reevaluation of Human and Mammalian Toxic Equivalency Factors for Dioxins and Dioxin-Like Compounds. Toxicological science 93(2):223–241; 
							https://doi.org/10.1093/toxsci/kfl055
						. Determined by means of 20-hour Soxhlet extraction with toluene or accelerated solvent extraction.

in surface waters and in a 3m-wide strip alongside surface waters, whereby the strip alongside watercourses for which a space for waters has been specified in accordance with Article 41a WPO
SR 814.201 or for which a space for waters has been expressly dispensed with under 41a paragraph 5 WPO is measured from the shore line, and in the case of other watercourses and standing waters from the top edge of the bank in accordance with the buffer strip information sheet «Measuring and managing buffers strips correctly», KIP/PIOCH 2009
The information sheet may be obtained (not in English) from Agridea, 8315 Lindau. ;

the substance or preparation fulfils the criteria of standard D 4359-90

 The standard may be viewed free of charge and obtained for a fee from the Swiss Association for Standardisation, Sulzerallee 70, 8404 Winterthur; www.snv.ch.
